keywords:
  - exoplanets
  - target prioritization
  - atmospheric characterization
  - JWST
  - ELT
  - Monte Carlo
  - Sobol sensitivity analysis
abstract: >
  Monte Carlo framework that turns NASA Exoplanet Archive uncertainties
  into per-facility (JWST transiting, ELT/PCS reflected light) and
  per-class (rocky, Hycean) priority lists for atmospheric
  characterization, combining climate, cumulative XUV atmospheric
  retention, per-draw composition and detectability. Version 6.1 adds a
  converged Saltelli-Sobol analysis (N = 512) for the rocky branch; the
  Hycean branch is released as indicative because its sensitivity
  analysis does not converge.
